[Narrator]
Scrrrrk... scrrrrk... scrrrrk...

[Jet]
!?

[Narrator]
You're startled by a sudden, strange sound coming from downstairs. 

Scrrrrk... scrrrrk... scrrrrk...

Something is scratching at the front door, frantically trying to get in.

[Jet]
There's no way anything's out there. Not in this weather.

Can't believe I'm hearing stuff now.

I just need to ignor–

[Cat]
Mrowwww!

[Narrator]
A sharp whine echoes throughout the house, followed shortly by another, more desperate cry that shakes you.

[Cat]
Mrowwwwww!!!

[Jet]
I've gotta go shut that noise up or else I'll get no rest tonight.

[Narrator]
You inch towards the door and peer through the peephole to see what's causing the commotion.

Rain is pouring down with so much force that it might as well be hail.

Between the downpour and the dark, you can barely see a few feet ahead.

[Cat]
Miauuuu!

[Narrator]
You're startled once again.

There's no mistaking it; the sound is coming from the foot of the door outside. 

You steel yourself, grab the handle and, with a twist of your wrist, open it slowly.

[Cat]
Meow.

[Jet]
Oh my god, you poor thing...

[Narrator]
You kneel down to get on the cat's level.

[Jet]
You lost, little guy? Hiding from the rain?

[Narrator]
As you run your hand over his drenched fur, you notice a yellow collar around his neck with a little pendant.

You inspect it more closely to find that the phone number and address on the back have worn away, leaving only the cat’s name on the front:

[Jet]
Pizza.

[Jet]
Pizza? Seriously? I've heard of 'Cookie' and 'Miso'. Even met a 'Ginger' (now that I think about it, I guess they named her after the color, not the spice). But Pizza?

[Pizza]
Miau?

[Narrator]
Pizza turns his head away from you, freeing the pendant from your hand, before inviting himself in.

[Jet]
Hey, no no no! You can't just..., your paws are all...

[Narrator]
The cat ignores your pleas completely, and instead moseys his way to your couch, leaving paw prints in his wake.

After a graceful little pounce, Pizza curls up in a shivering ball at the corner of the couch. 

You watch as he desperately tries to dry himself against the cushions to no avail.

[Pizza]
Mew...

[Jet]
Fine... okay, alright. You can stay the night, but not like that. I'll go get you a towel of mine from the bathroom.{setprogress 2}
